{
  "what_this_is": "Survey of the odometer cohort (solve.progress.source == 'odometer', the exact shape that makes clear_reachability's coord check structurally DEAD) for whether ppu::odo_blank / odometer_scene (clear_detect.SceneCutSignal, one of the six shelf signals wired 2026-08-26) can fire at all, and whether that firing survives a debounced death classifier. Not a clear-detection result: no profile here has solve.clear.mode set, so is_clear()/solutions is unchanged for all of them -- this only moves scene_cut from DEAD to ALIVE in clear_reachability.clear_quorum's eligibility table.",
  "methodology": "Per profile: 3 rollouts x 4000 frame_skip-steps (12,000 total) of a mixed-random policy biased toward the profile's own declared progress axis, from the profile's own start state. odo_blank and odometer_scene are edge-detected into runs each rollout. Where the profile declares a real `lives` address (0 is treated as the documented 'not yet discovered' placeholder, same shape as level_key: []), each run is classified death-class if it falls within 2 observations of a DEBOUNCED (>=3 consecutive dropped-lives observations) death state, else txn-candidate. No RAM map beyond what each profile already declares for other purposes (the same `lives` address RoomFpTransitionSignal's own death veto already consumes).",
  "scope_limit": "A short random/heuristic rollout can, for nearly every game on this roster, only reach a boot blackout and a handful of deaths -- real level transitions gate behind exactly the kind of search this project runs Go-Explore for. 'ARM' records that the counter is alive (moved, with a clean or death-only null) for that profile, NOT that a real transition has been witnessed on tape. Rygar is the sole exception with an independent skilled trajectory to check against (see rygar_cross_check below).",
  "rygar_excluded_by_design": "Rygar is a member of this cohort (solve.progress.source: odometer) but configs/rygar.yaml is deliberately NOT armed here. commit 51fbd528 (this same night) shipped scripts/transition_witness.py -- a Rygar-specific instrument built on the same odo_blank counter, calibrated far more tightly than this survey's generic architectural floor (a measured 40-blank-frame run-length gate vs. the 14-frame death fade and 78-79-frame door, plus a >=3-observation lives debounce and novelty memory against the re-anchor-ratchet double-count) -- and tests/test_transition_witness.py / test_rygar_r1_tape.py assert configs/rygar.yaml carries NO `clear`/`finale` key at all, specifically because docs/receipts/rygar/clear_predicate_REFUTED.md found every predicate available fabricates wins on Rygar's own deepest banked tape. Arming scene_cut here (even eligibility-only, no `mode`) would violate that guard's letter for no measured benefit -- Rygar already has the sharper, purpose-built instrument. tests/test_scene_cut_signal.py's own Rygar-tape test validates THIS module's SceneCutSignal death veto and n_events collapse against the same real tape without touching the profile's YAML at all.",
  "rygar_cross_check": "clear_detect.SceneCutSignal (this module, generic across the six-signal shelf) replayed against the same banked R1 tape (docs/receipts/rygar/r1_tape_gx6242.json) independently reproduces transition_witness.py's own numbers: 0 death vetoes (none of the tape's 55 two-observation lives blips reaches the 3-observation debounce), n_triggers in the hundreds (the raw stride-check tally the campaign warns against citing as a room count), and n_events (a rising edge of the held-pulse vote) collapsing to a handful across the whole tape -- see tests/test_scene_cut_signal.py::test_the_real_rygar_ratchet_collapses_to_a_handful_of_events_not_54.",
